{"_meta":{"as_of":"2026-10-26T18:52:29+00:00","coverage":"13/13","note":"Earnings dates and consensus from Yahoo Finance \u2014 often estimated rather than company-confirmed, so treat them as approximate until close. Policy and catalyst entries are hand-dated in the research files."},"events":[{"d":"2026-07-28","type":"policy","t":"LIVE \u2014 FCC Covered List now bars foreign-produced robots (Jul 28, 2026)","why":"Adopted, not proposed. Any ground-moving device over 4.4lb (with dock) that senses, connects and navigates cannot get FCC equipment authorisation unless the Department of War grants a Conditional Approval. Read the carve-outs before pricing it: industrial robotic ARMS, medical robots, vehicles and drones are explicitly excluded, so Fanuc, Yaskawa, ABB, KUKA/Midea, Estun and Doosan's cobots are untouched. What is caught is humanoids, quadrupeds and autonomous mobile robots \u2014 9880.HK UBTech head-on, 277810.KQ Rainbow Robotics and TER's MiR unit on the same terms despite being allied, plus 1810.HK Xiaomi's consumer line. HSAI is hit second-hand through its customers' US market access. The asymmetry is the point: US-produced humanoids get a market cleared by rule, everyone else queues for a discretionary exemption.","hits":"act, sen"},{"d":"2026-08-04","type":"policy","t":"Chinese WFE tools qualifying at Samsung and SK Hynix","why":"Reuters, Aug 4 2026: both Korean memory makers have been testing AMEC etch tools for their China fabs \u2014 begun ~2 years ago, aimed at SERVICING and upgrading existing lines rather than adding capacity, after Washington revoked their validated-end-user status in 2025 and replaced it with an annual licence. Small in units, large in meaning: qualification is the slow half of the WFE moat, and it is being done by the two customers whose sign-off other buyers copy. Deutsche Bank has NAURA, AMEC, Piotech and ACM Research each clearing $1B of revenue in 2026 and together taking 25-30% of China's ~$28B WFE market. This is the external bear case (see Thesis) arriving as an event rather than an opinion \u2014 watch whether qualification stays confined to China fabs.","hits":"wfe"},{"d":"2026-09-30","type":"catalyst","t":"800-volt DC racks \u2014 first volume shipments","why":"Opens the SiC/GaN power-chip story: Infineon, onsemi, Navitas, Delta, Lite-On.","hits":"Power & Cooling"},{"d":"2026-09-30","type":"catalyst","t":"Unitree IPO prices on the STAR board","why":"The first real public-market test of humanoid-maker economics.","hits":"Humanoid Robotics"},{"d":"2026-10-15","type":"catalyst","t":"TSMC Q3 report \u2014 does capex fear break?","why":"The best sentiment gauge for the whole AI supply chain \u2014 and the catalyst on our #1 entry window.","hits":"Foundry & Packaging"},{"d":"2026-10-21","type":"earnings","tk":"LRCX","n":"Lam Research","conv":2,"froth":1,"eps":2.35,"eps_lo":2.33,"eps_hi":2.55,"dd":-46.8,"ts":1792612800,"when":"post","xt":"16:00 EDT","rep":{"act":2.2,"est":2.18,"when":"2026-10-21","surp":0.9,"move":-0.02,"live":true,"post":-0.28},"wire":{"cues":[],"heads":[{"t":"No surprises in Lam Research\u2019s (NASDAQ:LRCX) Q3 sales numbers but stock drops","u":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMingFBVV95cUxPWFA2TGRyelJfZDlwMkhqQ21nUFE5cUR4c3JVMlJpZS1JbWJvZUNCbmNuS1dOTVpqemhRTk9mek9HZElWUjdERWt2NTRLZGtCeFFMWi1rV2RtTVg4TTd0bjloRlVTRmlJUGg0MUpaLUNxY245M2hsYUZsa3BTLXFPWVhHbEsxNU8ySjJFXy1scWM4RnhZWkFjQWZJT3JNUQ?oc=5","d":"2026-10-21","s":"Yahoo Finance"},{"t":"Lam Research Corporation Reports Financial Results for the Quarter Ended September 27, 2026","u":"https://news.google.?oc=5","d":"2026-10-21","s":"PR Newswire"},{"t":"Lam Research slides even as Q1 results and guidance top Wall Street's forecast (LRCX:NASDAQ)","u":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitgFBVV95cUxNRm1QY01fUzAtY2czWFVuYUxFYnJ4emNTZW9wUXhSVTVEdGxMRFdOV0RDa3NpUTN5MkpTWkYwME5nQmFKTXVEWGYwS3lfTXRjTXE4dDZlWUs5ZEFWNXM5aVdBaWhOcVVpUGs5VVJlT1JJQk9XZFYtNkpDOUNvS1YzeDZrNFYxVFVLYXhIUTdUTnByWjZpUTN4YVRUN19JUUh1M2s4NW